  "result": "Perfect! All 68 tests pass. Here's what I added:\n\n**`src/numbering.js`** \u2014 invoice number generation\n- `nextInvoiceNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)` calculates the next free number\n- Format: `INV-<year>-<counter>` (e.g., `INV-2026-0001`)\n- Counter is 4 digits, zero-padded, starts at 0001, resets each year\n- Handles unordered existing numbers by finding the max counter for the year\n- Validates date is real and in `YYYY-MM-DD` format (returns `DATE_INVALID`)\n- Prevents counter overflow (returns `TOO_MANY_INVOICES` if exceeds 9999)\n- Ignores malformed numbers\n\n**`issueInvoice(invoice, existingNumbers)`** in `src/invoices.js`\n- Issues a draft invoice, assigning it the next free number\n- Changes status from `'draft'` to `'issued'`\n- Returns `NOT_DRAFT` if invoice isn't in draft status\n- Preserves all invoice data (customerId, issueDate, lines, etc.)\n- Never mutates the input invoice\n- Propagates numbering errors (like `DATE_INVALID`, `TOO_MANY_INVOICES`)\n\n**Tests** (20 new: 12 for numbering, 8 for issuing) cover:\n- First invoice of a year and incrementing\n- Multiple years with separate counters\n- Unordered and large existing numbers\n- Date validation (format and reality)\n- Edge cases (9999 limit, malformed numbers, non-draft invoices)\n- Data preservation and non-mutation",
